  <div class="prose">
    <p class="lede">He is an Italian-Irish writer, screenwriter and director based in Cork,
    working across film, TV and audio.</p>

    <p>He is <strong>Head of Story at True Story Studios</strong>, the boutique development
    company he runs with screenwriter <strong>David Aaron Cohen</strong>. He is also the author
    of the urban fantasy novel <em>Dead Men Naked</em>.</p>
    {# TODO (Dario): add David's two best-known credits here in parentheses. Claire left them
       out rather than guess them wrong. #}

    <p>His scripts have gone to the Austin Film Festival as a Semifinalist and a Quarter-Finalist.
    His short film <em>Trigger Warning</em> screened internationally, from Rio de Janeiro to Tokyo.
    His audio dramas <em>Strati</em> and <em>The Secret Seas of Puglia</em> were commissioned by
    the Italian Cultural Authority and the Puglia Region.</p>

    <p>He writes about the numinous arriving through the neglected — the derelict door that still
    opens, the vessel that runs on spirit rather than fuel. Dark humour, and always a
    philosophical spin. He reads Camus, Jung, Vallée and Pasulka, and he is drawn to structures
    that turn round in the third act and quietly rewrite everything you thought you had understood.</p>
  </div>

